lessons (relation-root-qualification): 12 live; adopted first. Status is derived from tests.
- [adopted +98/-0] L-77b44d3fe205 (*): when writing or editing a PR body -> run python3 tools/pcc/pcc.py lint-prose --stdin on it before submitting; reword claim words for proposals or cite [pcc:ID]
- [adopted +55/-0] L-1e09e78e395f (*): when writing today's session log -> fetch origin/main first and append to the existing same-day file; other sessions write the same file and an add/add conflict blocks merge
- [adopted +24/-1] L-8d86e8fc352c (*): when correcting a results file whose hash a VALIDATION.json or validator report pins -> leave the pinned file byte-equal and put the corrections in a sibling ERRATA.md that the PROOF/problem notes cite; editing it in place makes the gate report a sha256 mismatch
- [adopted +22/-0] L-5b0291c61e8e (*): when Merging an append-only shared journal with repeated section headings -> Compare and preserve full normalized blocks as a multiset, retaining their multiplicities; headings are not unique keys. Preserve existing chronology and review source pins before applying a prepared merge.
- [adopted +9/-0] L-03e1d0d51c4d (*): when Creating a PCC claim in a fresh sparse checkout -> Materialize the tracked pcc ledger and keyring from the pinned base before invoking claim new; verify the base prefix before publication.
- [adopted +4/-0] L-d5062ba05212 (*): when A UTC rollover creates or edits a dated journal outside a custom sparse-checkout definition -> Use git add --sparse for that journal and verify its staged diff and committed contents before pushing;a tracked path can still require --sparse on later edits.
- [candidate +1/-0] L-97bc69de5096 (*): when fixing the first failing step of a CI job that has been red for a while -> expect later steps to have been masked: after the fix lands, read the next run's log to the end before calling the job fixed
- [candidate +1/-0] L-aaadbdbf3b2a (*): when binding an ecbench instrument commit for a frozen protocol or queue registration -> build target/release/ecbench at that exact commit and run ecbench plan on the specs before freezing; main 3b0840b6f2 did not compile (retained_chain_study.rs missed the new PrimeInstance.representation field) and no PR check caught it
- [candidate +0/-0] L-dbdd5a9d8530 (*): when restarting a work branch whose PR merged with a merge commit -> git checkout -B <branch> origin/main (carry uncommitted work with git stash) and push normally: the old remote head is an ancestor of main, so the push fast-forwards; no force push is needed
- [candidate +0/-0] L-306254ce1b4a (*): when a generator scans a file that also contains its own generated output (e.g. tools/artifacts/wire_workflows.py and the pull step it writes into workflows) -> strip the generated block before discovery and declare indirect inputs explicitly; otherwise an entry the tool once wrote counts as a reference to itself and never drops out
- [candidate +0/-0] L-85f1696fa884 (*): when editing or writing tests in a Rust source file that another crate includes with #[path] (e.g. src/binary_ecc/f2m.rs in research/quadratic_twist_evidence_20261021/native/metadata) -> use relative super:: paths, never crate::<module>:: paths, and build the including crate too
- [candidate +0/-0] L-144e025d7380 (*): when Comparing to origin/main in a reused sparse worktree with a custom remote fetch refspec -> Fetch refs/heads/main explicitly to refs/remotes/origin/main and verify its SHA matches the intended remote main before ledger/keyring checks or diffs; prefer exact-path or name-only diffs.
